    // that flag raised for the rest of the page. Every later render then
    // turned back at it and never asked again, and the rejection escaped the
    // pane unhandled. The picker is the room's strongest privacy control made
    // easy to use, and one transient failure removed it until she reloaded.
    //
    // ⛔ THE RESET IS THE WHOLE FIX, AND ITS RELATIONSHIP TO THE THIRD
    // GUARD IS WHY IT IS ENOUGH. That guard remembers, for the page session,
    // an answer of NO FOLDERS — deliberately, because an answer is worth
    // remembering. ⛔ A FAILURE IS NOT AN ANSWER, and must not be
    // remembered the same way. Releasing the in-flight flag is precisely what
    // keeps the two apart: the answer is kept, the failure is not.
    //
    // ⛔ AND IT SAYS NOTHING. That silence is hers, in writing: if the
    // room could not read her vault — or asked and got no answer — it
    // says nothing (26.96-KNOWN-LIMITATIONS.md § 11). So this side may not
    // mark the read as having been ANSWERED, because her no-folders sentence
